# Security headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# Copied verbatim into dist/ at build time and read by Cloudflare Pages, which
# serves tlbelectric.ca. GitHub Pages (the /TLBv2 preview built by
# .github/workflows/deploy.yml) ignores this file — GH Pages cannot set custom
# headers, so the preview will always score worse than production. Expected.
#
# FORMAT WARNING: a rule is a path line followed by indented header lines, and
# anything that reads as a blank line ends the rule. Do not put comments or
# blank lines INSIDE a block — an indented comment can strip to whitespace and
# silently truncate every header after it. All notes therefore live up here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Origins allowed by the CSP, and why each is needed:
#
#   fonts.googleapis.com   Google Fonts stylesheet             Layout.astro
#   fonts.gstatic.com      the woff2 files that stylesheet pulls
#   images.unsplash.com    hero background image               Hero.astro
#   w.behold.so            Instagram widget script             InstagramFeed.astro
#   feeds.behold.so        the feed JSON that widget fetches
#   behold.pictures        Behold's image CDN
#   *.cdninstagram.com     Instagram media served into the feed
#   api.web3forms.com      quote form submission               ContactForm.astro
#   maps.google.com        map iframe — MapEmbed.astro is commented out of
#                          index.astro today, but is pre-allowed so re-enabling
#                          it does not silently break against this policy
#
# Cloudflare's own /cdn-cgi/ email-obfuscation script is same-origin, so 'self'
# already covers it.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-header notes for the /* block below:
#
#   Strict-Transport-Security  Forces HTTPS for a year. Drop includeSubDomains
#                              if a subdomain is ever served over plain HTTP.
#                              `preload` is omitted deliberately — it means
#                              submitting to the browser preload list and is
#                              painful to reverse.
#   X-Frame-Options            Clickjacking. frame-ancestors in the CSP is the
#                              modern equivalent and wins where both are
#                              understood; this covers older browsers.
#   X-Content-Type-Options     Already set by Cloudflare, restated so the whole
#   Referrer-Policy            policy lives in one place.
#   Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy Severs the opener relationship for windows this
#                              site opens (the Google review links). Those
#                              already carry rel="noopener"; this enforces it.
#   Cross-Origin-Resource-     Stops other origins embedding our assets from a
#   Policy                     browser context. Overridden for og-image.png.
#   ! Access-Control-Allow-    Cloudflare Pages defaults every response to
#     Origin                   `Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`. Nothing here is
#                              fetched cross-origin, so drop it rather than
#                              advertise a wide-open CORS policy.
#
# Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy is deliberately NOT set. `require-corp` would
# block the Unsplash hero and every Instagram image, since those origins do not
# send CORP headers. The scanner lists it as "upcoming"; it is not safe here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# On 'unsafe-inline':
#
# Astro emits component scripts and JSON-LD blocks inline, and several
# components use inline style="" attributes. CSP hashes cover inline <script>
# and <style> ELEMENTS but not style ATTRIBUTES, so a hash-only policy silently
# breaks things like the contact form's display:none success/error divs.
# Tightening this means refactoring the inline style attributes out first, then
# enabling Astro's `security.csp` option to generate per-page hashes.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), autoplay=(), browsing-topics=(), camera=(), display-capture=(), encrypted-media=(), fullscreen=(self), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), midi=(), payment=(), picture-in-picture=(), publickey-credentials-get=(), screen-wake-lock=(), usb=(), xr-spatial-tracking=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  ! Access-Control-Allow-Origin
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'self'; form-action 'self' https://api.web3forms.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://w.behold.so; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data: https://images.unsplash.com https://behold.pictures https://*.cdninstagram.com; connect-src 'self' https://api.web3forms.com https://feeds.behold.so; frame-src https://maps.google.com https://www.google.com; manifest-src 'self'; upgrade-insecure-requests

/og-image.png
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: cross-origin
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800

/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
